{"id":"39.3.5","doc":"T","title":"ADC Conversion and Attenuation","words":115,"blocks":[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":1,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"When the SAR ADCs convert an analog voltage, the resolution ("},{"t":"num","v":"12-bit","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":") of the conversion spans voltage range from "},{"t":"num","v":"0 mV","k":"voltage"},{"t":"text","v":" to V"},{"t":"sub","v":"ref"},{"t":"text","v":"."}]},{"n":2,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"V"},{"t":"sub","v":"ref"},{"t":"text","v":" is the "},{"t":"block","v":"SAR ADC","id":"adc"},{"t":"text","v":"'s internal reference voltage ("},{"t":"num","v":"1100 mV","k":"voltage"},{"t":"text","v":" by design)."}]},{"n":3,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The output value of the conversion (data) is mapped to analog voltage V"},{"t":"sub","v":"data"},{"t":"text","v":" using the following formula:"}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":4,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"V"},{"t":"sub","v":"data"},{"t":"text","v":" = (V"},{"t":"sub","v":"ref"},{"t":"text","v":" / k) × (data / 4095)"}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":5,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"k is the coefficient corresponding to the configured attenuation."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":6,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"In order to convert voltages larger than V"},{"t":"sub","v":"ref"},{"t":"text","v":", input signals can be attenuated before being input into the SAR ADCs."}]},{"n":7,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The supported attenuation levels are:"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":8,"c":[{"t":"num","v":"0 dB","k":"other"},{"t":"text","v":" (k≈"},{"t":"num","v":"100%","k":"other"},{"t":"text","v":")"}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":9,"c":[{"t":"num","v":"2.5 dB","k":"other"},{"t":"text","v":" (k≈"},{"t":"num","v":"75%","k":"other"},{"t":"text","v":")"}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":10,"c":[{"t":"num","v":"6 dB","k":"other"},{"t":"text","v":" (k≈"},{"t":"num","v":"50%","k":"other"},{"t":"text","v":")"}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":11,"c":[{"t":"num","v":"12 dB","k":"other"},{"t":"text","v":" (k≈"},{"t":"num","v":"25%","k":"other"},{"t":"text","v":"